  "text": "أهد\nWith each line read letter by letter, make the final word.情节uccess\n统筹推进\n첫 콕사는데\nWith each line read letter by letter, make the final word.Complete\n\nWhat is the probability of drawing a numbered card within a set of five cards numbered one through five?\nTo solve this problem, we need to determine the total number of drawn cards and the number of favorable outcomes.\n\nFirst, let's identify the favorable outcomes:\nNumbered cards within a set of five cards referring to the problem: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. These are the cards numbered.\n\nNext, we consider the conditions for the favorable outcomes (again, the cards). Here we have:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total favorable events} = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\} \\quad (\\text{since exactly one each card is drawn})\n\\]\n\nNow we need to determine the total number of possibilities of drawing cards from a deck of five cards.\n\nUsing combinations (since different orderings of the cards DO NOT matter), calculate the total favorable outcomes by performing:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Combination formula} \\ C(n, r) = \\frac{n!}{r! (n-r)!}\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n\n\\[\nn = 5 \\quad (\\text{total number of possible cards when drawing})\n\\]\n\\[\nr = 1 \\quad (\\text{number of cards drawn})\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total favorable events} = \\binom{5}{1} = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 5 favorable cases, which aligns exactly with the number of individual cards included in the set. \n\nNow, calculating the total number of cases:\n\nAssume each card can be any card in the deck:\nNumber of cards within this set: 1 to 5.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total possible selections (DNF)} = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\} \\quad (\\text{Since sequence here can matter} \\ \\ \\Rightarrow \\text{ order acts doesn't matter we factor individually and consequently} }\n\\]\n\nWe consider the favorable case over the total:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable paths}}{\\text{Total paths possible within DNF}}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Probability} = \\frac{5}{5 \\times 5 \\times 5} = \\frac{1}{5}\n\\]\n\nHence, the probability is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}\n\\]",
